name very_low_capacity
describe 100 kbps link (audio 32 kbps + video): the stage-1 checkpoint for very low capacity
# sm_compare runs 80 seeds here (#437): after #435's NACK port the 10-seed freeze-count cell
# (24.9 vs 21.3, behind on 8/10) may be seed spread, as the #420 and #409 cells were; 80 seeds place it.
compare_seeds 80
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=100kbps delay=30ms queue=300ms
# Checkpoint for issue #74 (roadmap #64). The expect lines lock in what main does
# today on seeds 1-5 (the worst seed is in the comment); they are not targets.
# The stage-1 target is libwebrtc's behaviour on this link, which sm_compare
# (CI compare-webrtc) reports once this scenario is on main.
# Seeds 1-5 on main when this was added: concealed 12.0-15.2 %, render fps 0.9-1.5,
# loss 34.1-36.7 %, keyframe requests 194-235, send over target the whole call.
# Target (issue #74): video.render_fps > 5, audio.concealed_pct < 3,
# net.loss_pct < 10, cc.send_over_target_ms < 5000, keyframe requests near 0.
expect video.render_fps > 0.5
expect audio.concealed_pct < 20
expect net.loss_pct < 45
expect video.keyframe_requests < 300
